FOMO'a

814
00:57:52,947 --> 00:57:57,147
GCF Global, creating opportunities for a better life.

815
00:57:58,187 --> 00:58:03,047
This. You log into social media and you see this picture of some friends at a party.

816
00:58:03,967 --> 00:58:07,268
Scroll down and here's a video of a friend cliff diving in Cancun.

817
00:58:08,147 --> 00:58:12,288
A number of friends are talking about Garden Cop and you haven't seen it yet.

818
00:58:12,847 --> 00:58:18,127
And now you start feeling something called FOMO, or fear of missing out.

819
00:58:18,127 --> 00:58:25,487
FOMO is the anxiety we experience when we feel there's something exciting happening elsewhere and we're not a part of it.

820
00:58:25,788 --> 00:58:31,708
It's been around for a long time, but these days it's triggered mostly by posts on social media.

821
00:58:32,987 --> 00:58:36,748
Social media gives us instant access to the activity of our friends.

822
00:58:37,187 --> 00:58:38,387
That's what it's there for.

823
00:58:38,987 --> 00:58:45,167
And this can be a good thing, but it also makes it all too easy for us to compare our lives to theirs.

824
00:58:45,167 --> 00:58:50,147
This can lead us to second guessing our decisions and feeling insecure in general.

825
00:58:50,708 --> 00:58:55,687
It can even get to the point when there's a looming sense of FOMO, even when we're not online.

826
00:58:56,567 --> 00:58:58,167
So how do we kick this FOMO?

827
00:58:58,807 --> 00:59:03,248
An answer that might quickly spring to mind is to simply quit social media.

828
00:59:03,927 --> 00:59:06,367
But that's not practical for a lot of people.

829
00:59:07,327 --> 00:59:12,147
Instead of quitting, you can try limiting your time on it or even just taking a few days off.

830
00:59:12,147 --> 00:59:19,127
This can give you a chance to focus on what's important in your life and enjoy the things that you are doing without comparing them to others.

831
00:59:20,288 --> 00:59:23,947
The lives of our friends do sometimes look pretty exciting online.

832
00:59:24,447 --> 00:59:27,567
But let's put some quotation marks around the word lives.

833
00:59:28,127 --> 00:59:31,607
Their social media activity isn't their actual life per se.

834
00:59:31,967 --> 00:59:36,887
It's more of a highlight reel of exciting things they've posted to contribute to their online identity.

835
00:59:36,887 --> 00:59:39,707
It's easy to see these highlights and think,

836
00:59:40,467 --> 00:59:43,687
my life just isn't as exciting as theirs.

837
00:59:44,627 --> 00:59:48,467
But what we're usually not seeing is what's going on behind the scenes.

838
00:59:48,947 --> 00:59:52,527
The negative things or the boring routine of their day-to-day lives.

839
00:59:53,067 --> 00:59:58,327
They may post something awesome, but in the grand scheme of things, it's just a short snippet of their day.

840
00:59:58,327 --> 01:00:05,827
The odds are, when they're not out doing these awesome things, they probably experience just as much FOMO as you do.

841
01:00:05,827 --> 01:00:17,827
